### create gate is live — task new without --body/--ac must be refused (exit 2)
$ env -i HOME=/tmp/tm-082-y6A2cW/home PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin TERM=dumb bash -c 'cd "/tmp/tm-082-y6A2cW/consumer" && ./.bytedesk/task-management/bin/tm epic new "First epic"'
EP-001 created and set active — /tmp/tm-082-y6A2cW/consumer/.bytedesk/task-management/epics/EP-001-first-epic.md
(exit 0)
$ env -i HOME=/tmp/tm-082-y6A2cW/home PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin TERM=dumb bash -c 'cd "/tmp/tm-082-y6A2cW/consumer" && ./.bytedesk/task-management/bin/tm task new "bare task"'
task-management: new tasks carry their details from birth — missing:
  body — tm edit <id> --body
  acceptance — tm ac <id> "…"
Or supply them at creation: .bytedesk/task-management/bin/tm task new "<title>" --body <text|-> --ac "<criterion>"
Bypass once: .bytedesk/task-management/bin/tm override "<reason>"
(exit 2)

